From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:30:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: Make bus-npu a child of ahb-npu

The NPU has a gate in the AHB matrix (ahb-npu) and one in its own bus
gating reset register (bus-npu). Its register interface needs both:
with either of them off, the registers of the NPU read as zero. The
vivante,gc binding has one clock for the register interface, so a
consumer can hold only one of them.

The manual does not name a parent for bus-npu, so the hosc parent taken
from the vendor BSP is a guess as well. Make bus-npu a child of
ahb-npu. Enabling bus-npu then enables ahb-npu.

Not covered: the rate of bus-npu, which has no consumer.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; bus-npu sits under
ahb-npu and both gates are on while the NPU is awake; switching either
of them off by hand makes the registers read as zero.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
index 78b0579a82b7..8895da5350e0 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60i-a733.c
@@ -13,7 +13,7 @@
  * known kernel consumer, so they are not modelled here.
  *
  * TODO: The real parents of some bus gates, including its-pcie0-aclk,
- * msi-lite, npu, sgpio, lpc and i2spcm, are not documented in the
+ * msi-lite, sgpio, lpc and i2spcm, are not documented in the
  * manual. For now, follow the vendor BSP, which keeps them on hosc.
  */
 
@@ -895,7 +895,13 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_M_HW_WITH_MUX_GATE(npu_clk, "npu", npu_parents, 0xb00,
 				    24, 3,	/* mux */
 				    BIT(31),	/* gate */
 				    0);
-static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_DATA(bus_npu_clk, "bus-npu", hosc, 0xb04, BIT(0), 0);
+/*
+ * The NPU has a gate in the AHB matrix and one in its own bus gating reset
+ * register. The NPU binding has one clock for both, so the second gate is
+ * the parent of the first: enabling bus-npu enables ahb-npu too.
+ */
+static const struct clk_hw *ahb_npu_hws[] = { &ahb_npu_clk.common.hw };
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_npu_clk, "bus-npu", ahb_npu_hws, 0xb04, BIT(0), 0);
 
 /*
  * GPU_CLK = ClockSource * ((16 - M) / 16)
